{
  "summary": "The RNA-only, single-profile scVI_n200 configuration achieved validation accuracy 0.5203 and F1 0.4982, exceeding the prior RNA-only PCA_n2000 baseline of 0.4849 accuracy and 0.4639 F1. This initial comparison suggests that a learned RNA representation may provide a modest improvement over PCA in this setting, though the encoder dimensionality differs and the result does not establish a causal mechanism. It remains uncertain whether the gain reflects scVI specifically, the 200-dimensional representation, or other uncontrolled factors."
}

